## Frontend Architecture Law

### State Management

- Always import stores from `@/store` (barrel at `frontend/src/store/index.ts`).
- Never import a store file directly (e.g. `from '@/store/soundscapeStore'`).
- See `zustand-stores.mdc` for how to add or modify stores.

### API Calls

- All backend calls use `fetchWithErrorHandling()` from `frontend/src/services/api.ts`.
- Always include `credentials: 'include'` (session cookie auth).
- Add typed methods to the `apiService` object — never call raw `fetch` for backend routes.

### Styling

- Colors via CSS custom properties from `frontend/src/app/globals.css` only.
- Never write hex, rgba, or named colors in component files or `constants.ts`.
- Tailwind classes (`text-primary`, `bg-secondary-light`, `shadow-md`) work via `@theme inline` in `globals.css`.
- Card vertical spacing is token-driven (`--card-space-*` / `--card-gap-*` + `.card-shell`,
  `.card-stack*`, `.card-field*`, `.card-label`, `.card-collapse-body` in `globals.css`). Never add
  ad-hoc `space-y-*`/`mb-*`/`px-*` spacing to card content — Card owns the inset.
- See `ui-conventions.mdc` for Three.js / Canvas 2D color patterns and the Card rhythm tokens.

### TypeScript

- Strict mode. `pnpm build` (from `frontend/`) must pass with 0 errors before any commit.
- No `any`. Use type assertions only at verified system boundaries with an explanatory comment.
- Path alias: always `@/*` → `src/*`. Avoid relative `../../` imports more than one level up.
- Domain types in `src/types/<domain>.ts`, exported from `src/types/index.ts`.

